'''Kappy Kawano''' (川野かわわっぱ, ''Kawano Kawawappa'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Invasion of the Swamplord]]. He was added in [[Version 12.5 Update|Version 12.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Kappy Kawano
|image = E 653.png
|appearance = [[Invasion of the Swamplord]]
|money drop = 2,500¢ - 9,875¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy works very much like [[Kappy Jr.]] He has massive health and deals extreme damage at mid-range split into three closely-spaced multi-hits, each causing a [[Surge Attack]] that can hit much further than Kawano himself. If that wasn't enough, he is immune to weaken and replicates any Surges hitting him, dealing damage equivalent to his first hit. He is slower, tougher and has fewer knockbacks, but there is still a significant delay between his attacks.

==Strategy==
Kappy Jr.'s old man may seem terrifying at first, with his great reach, very high damage, and the ability to spawn up to THREE Surge Attacks which can easily crush anything short of [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]]. However, Kappy Kawano's attack rate sits at a staggering 7 seconds, almost thrice of his son. This means that despite his immense damage, stalling this enemy isn't hard when he's by himself. Due to his decently long foreswing, you can potentially let the peons of the first three stages push a little bit to try and make him miss, but don't rely on this as you can find yourself getting overwhelmed by them.

Any units with immunity to Surges can help immensely, both for stalling and damaging Kappy Kawano. Some great units to use for him are [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] and Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]].

Things get complicated in [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|Ghost King Finale]], where after the base is hit, a [[Golem Sunfish]] and Kawano himself will both spawn, with Kappy Jr. arriving after 60 seconds as well. Do as much damage as you can to Kawano before Jr. spawns, as the father-son duo will start pushing insanely hard once they are both on the field, especially with the Golem Sunfish occasionally nuking out your attackers.

